# Makefile Workflow

`make` is the only entry point for development tasks. Never use ad-hoc `go run`, `go build`, or `psql` directly.

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| First-time setup | `make setup` |
| Run dev server | `make run` |
| Compile binary | `make build` |
| Run tests | `make test` |
| Lint | `make lint` |
| Tidy dependencies | `make tidy` |
| Check environment | `make doctor` |
| Start Postgres | `make db-up` |
| Create database | `make db-create` |

After any code change: `make test` before declaring done.
After any dependency change: `make tidy`.
